{
  "name": "Parent Controller Workflow",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# PARENT CONTROLLER WORKFLOW\n## Self-Healing Architecture & Dead Letter Queue\n\n**Role:** Main orchestrator. Receives the initial payload, delegates business logic to the Worker, and centrally manages both successes and failures.\n\n### Flow:\n```\nWebhook ──► Execute Worker\n                ├── ✅ SUCCESS  ──► Respond 200 OK\n                └── ❌ FAILURE  ──► Notion DLQ\n                                        └──► Email Alert\n```\n\n### Architectural Principle:\n- **Separation of Concerns:** business logic lives in the Worker\n- **Zero Data Loss:** the original payload is always preserved\n- **Instant Observability:** immediate alert dispatched to the IT team",
        "height": 512,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "b71f8f14-0348-420f-a79e-6ac2b737350b",
      "name": "🏗️ Architecture Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1904,
        1072
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Payload Entry Point\n\nThe webhook receives the raw JSON payload (e.g. customer order, CRM lead).\n\n**Expected payload example:**\n```json\n{\n  \"customer_id\": \"CUST-001\",\n  \"email\": \"user@example.com\",\n  \"order_amount\": 1500.00,\n  \"product\": \"Enterprise Plan\"\n}\n```",
        "height": 356,
        "width": 340,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "1161f14a-ef47-4929-b388-8b8aec0257c5",
      "name": "📌 Step 1 — Webhook Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1280,
        1072
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Worker Execution\n\n**CRITICAL Configuration:**\n1. **Source:** Database → select `child-worker-workflow`\n2. **Wait for sub-workflow:** ✅ Enabled\n3. **On Error:** `Continue (using error output)` ✅\n\n\nThis configuration creates **two output branches:**\n- `Output 0` → success ✅\n- `Output 1` → error ❌\n\n\nThe original payload is always available as `$json` in both branches.",
        "height": 356,
        "width": 360,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "14232ce9-e953-413f-8f4a-b23f10a92d19",
      "name": "📌 Step 2 — Execute Worker",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -912,
        1072
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ✅ SUCCESS BRANCH\n\nThe Worker completed processing successfully.\n\nHere you can:\n- Reply to the webhook with `200 OK`\n- Update a status database\n- Send a confirmation to the customer\n- Trigger subsequent steps in the process",
        "height": 264,
        "width": 428,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "1b2d3f6d-16a6-4a31-a5b2-ae15bc13fbb1",
      "name": "✅ Success Branch",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -448,
        1072
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ❌ ERROR BRANCH — Dead Letter Queue\n\nThe Worker has failed. This branch:\n1. **Captures** the original payload + error message\n2. **Writes** to Notion as a DLQ entry\n3. **Notifies** the IT team via Email\n\n### Available data here:\n- `$json` → original payload, intact\n- `$json.error.message` → error message\n- `$json.error.stack` → full stack trace\n- `$execution.id` → n8n execution ID\n\n\n🔴 **Zero Data Loss guaranteed:** the payload is never lost even if the external API is down.",
        "height": 412,
        "width": 380,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "513dde13-9924-4a8e-b3b8-883845293488",
      "name": "❌ Error Branch — DLQ",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -480,
        1824
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Notion Dead Letter Queue\n\nCreates a Notion database entry with:\n- Serialized original payload\n- Error message\n- Stack trace\n- Failure timestamp\n- Direct link to the n8n execution\n\n\n**Required setup:**\n- Create a Notion database with columns: `Status`, `Payload`, `Error`, `Execution URL`, `Created At`\n- Insert the database ID in the `Database ID` field\n- Configure Notion credentials",
        "height": 408,
        "width": 360,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "04731000-a1c8-4c91-8d9f-0b2ba0ecd56b",
      "name": "Notion DLQ",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -64,
        1824
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Alert Email\n\nSends a diagnostic email to the IT team with:\n- Error type\n- Direct link to the failed execution\n- Original payload (for fast manual re-processing)\n- Precise timestamp\n\n\n**Required setup:**\n- Configure SMTP credentials\n- Update `toEmail` with the IT team address\n\n\n💡 Alternatively, use the **Slack** node to notify an `#alerts-engineering` channel",
        "height": 404,
        "width": 360,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "08ca71d0-2be7-42f5-9ec6-70f531860111",
      "name": "Email Alert",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        336,
        1824
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ⚙️ SETUP CHECKLIST\n\n**Before going to production:**\n\n- [ ] Import `child-worker-workflow.json` and copy its **Workflow ID**\n- [ ] Open the `Execute Worker Sub-Workflow` node and paste the Workflow ID\n- [ ] Create the Notion database with columns: `Status`, `Error Message`, `Stack Trace`, `Original Payload`, `Execution URL`, `Failed At`\n- [ ] Configure **Notion** credentials in the DLQ node\n- [ ] Configure **SMTP** credentials in the Email node\n- [ ] Update `toEmail` with the IT team's email address\n- [ ] Update `YOUR-N8N-HOST` with your n8n domain\n- [ ] Test by sending a payload to the webhook and verifying the DLQ entry",
        "height": 332,
        "width": 564,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "eb2d5ece-8456-494f-be58-3d91a945b0f9",
      "name": "⚙️ Setup Checklist",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1904,
        1648
      ]
    },
